(Title) Tj
T*
(Protocol for a Randomized Controlled Trial of Aggressive Beta-Blockade Strategies in Acute) Tj
T*
(Decompensated Cardiac Failure With Rapid Atrial Fibrillation) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Rapid ventricular response during atrial fibrillation in acute heart failure creates) Tj
T*
(hemodynamic stress and worsens clinical decompensation. This protocol evaluates whether a) Tj
T*
(protocolized approach using a potent beta-blocker combined with additional rate-limiting) Tj
T*
(agents achieves faster heart rate control and greater symptomatic relief compared to) Tj
T*
(conventional rate control strategies. We will enroll approximately 40 hospitalized) Tj
T*
(patients with acute heart failure, systolic dysfunction \(ejection fraction <35%\), and) Tj
T*
(atrial fibrillation with rapid ventricular response \(heart rate >130 beats per minute\).) Tj
T*
(Participants are randomly assigned to intensive rate control using beta-blockade plus) Tj
T*
(adjunctive agents or to standard therapy. Endpoints include time to achievement of target) Tj
T*
(heart rate, hemodynamic parameters, dyspnea scores, and adverse events over 24 hours of) Tj
T*
(observation.) Tj
ET
